> 1. What types of food do different types of pets like for treats?
> 

It depends on what type of pet it is.  There are 5 types of pets as far as
"treat" food is concerned: carnivore, herbivore, and omnivore,
metallivore, and non-eating. For carnivores, treats are: Tripe rations,
meatballs, meat ring, meat stick, and huge chunk of meat.  For herbivores,
treats are: apples and carrots.  Omnivores consider all of the carnivore &
herbivore treats to be treats.  Metallivores consider metallic, rust-prone
(iron, not rustproofed) objects to be treats.  Non-eating don't have
treats (I'm sure that's a big shock, but true none the less). There's also
a special check, and all of the 'Y' monsters consider bananas to be
treats.

> 2. How do I throw food to a pet? Is there like a special throw command,
> cause it won't let me throw food with the throw command, or do people
> say that when they mean just drop the food on the ground and let the
> animal get it?

Actually, you can throw food using the normal throw command, it just won't
list food items in your inventory when you press '?' at the prompt: you
can press '*' instead to get a full inventory listing, including food. But
you don't strictly have to throw the food, you can drop it and when your
pet eats it, it will have the same effect as if you threw it.  When your
pet eats something, it decides whether you were the one feeding it or not
by checking if the object has an inventory letter set, meaning it was ever
in the player's inventory.

You might be interested in the "Keeping And Training Pets In Nethack And
Slash'EM" spoiler, at:
<http://www.statslab.cam.ac.uk/~eva/nethack/pets2.html>

